Reachy Mini is a robot by Pollen Robotics and Hugging Face. reachy-bridge is an
independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by either company.

This product includes material from the following projects, both Copyright
Pollen Robotics and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

- reachy-mini (https://github.com/pollen-robotics/reachy_mini)
  web/src/assets/reachy_mini.glb and web/src/assets/reachy_mini.rig.json are
  derived from the MuJoCo model and meshes shipped in the reachy-mini Python
  package (reachy_mini/descriptions/reachy_mini/mjcf/). They were re-posed,
  merged per moving part, decimated and compressed; tools/model/ holds the
  scripts that produce them. Pollen Robotics publishes the robot's hardware
  design files separately under Creative Commons BY-NC-SA; this product does
  not include those files.

- Reachy Mini desktop app (https://github.com/pollen-robotics/reachy-mini-desktop-app)
  The emoji for recorded moves in web/src/logic/moves.ts are adapted from
  src/constants/choreographies.ts.

reachy-bridge does not bundle the reachy-mini daemon: deploy/install.sh
installs it from PyPI under its own license. The controller binary statically
links Rust crates and embeds a web dashboard built with npm packages; all of
them are under permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, Unicode-3.0,
Unlicense, BSL-1.0), and their notices travel with their sources as listed in
controller/Cargo.lock and web/bun.lock.
